  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"exploring intersections of the body, cloth, and language"--Page 3.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Text means Tissue is a collection of textiles and the written word, with a particular focus on femininity. Parallels between textile and feminine nature are numerous, and appear repeatedly throughout history and art ... Text means Tissue proposes that the articulation of ideas in cloth and writing are interchangeable as modes of feminine expression. Through this expanded use of language, the work in the collection creates a contemporary framework for a dialogue that women have been shaping for centuries"--Page 9.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book was designed, edited, and published by Francesca Capone. It was created on the occasion of the exhibition 'Text means Tissue' at Nationale in Portland, Oregon. February, 2017"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
